Link the bundled METIS (libmetis-gtsam) against libregex on QNX.

METIS carries GKlib, whose string helpers call regcomp/regexec/regfree;
QNX keeps those in libregex.so.1, not in libc. Without it
libmetis-gtsam.so records no NEEDED for libregex (shared libraries link
with undefined symbols allowed) and every program using GTSAM has to add
-lregex itself. Same fix as ports/gklib/patches/0002.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/gtsam/3rdparty/metis/libmetis/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/gtsam/3rdparty/metis/libmetis/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -8,6 +8,10 @@
 if(UNIX)
   target_link_libraries(metis-gtsam m)
 endif()
+if(QNX)
+  # GKlib's regex helpers use regcomp/regexec, which QNX keeps in libregex.
+  target_link_libraries(metis-gtsam regex)
+endif()
 
 if(WIN32)
 		set_target_properties(metis-gtsam PROPERTIES
